Body:
@jpgomezv 两条都收下：固定路径那条（你那台是 `WindowsApps` 别名，不是 System32）和 #50950 的"文件被删"猜测（你在脚本在位的情况下复现出同样文本，直接排除）。我已经改掉自己在 #50924 上的说法，并把 #51038 描述里那句 caveat 换成了这段更正。

你说的 `/c/Users/...` 细节和我的观察一致：我这台机器上 Git Bash 对原生 `C:\...` 参数是直接接受的（exit 0），所以问题从来不在路径写法，而在选中了哪个 shell —— 这也是 #51038 用候选 shell 自己的 `uname -s` 做过滤、完全不做路径转换的原因。

愿意做这个测试者，正好补上我缺的那块。改动在 `packages/cli/src/services/updater.ts`，分支 `Tsuki-hash:windows-installer-shell`（PR #51038，base `v2`）。我这边没法端到端验证：本机没装 Bun，而且真跑升级会动到我自己的安装。你机器上值得看的两个点是：Git 只在 `Git\cmd` 进 PATH 的情况下，安装脚本是否由 `C:\Program Files\Git\bin\bash.exe` 执行；以及把 Git 从 PATH 完全摘掉后，是否得到那条具名错误（提示装 Git for Windows 或设 `OPENCODE_GIT_BASH_PATH`），而不是现在的 127。

Fix-site correction after re-reading the current head, so the pointer is exact.

My earlier comment pointed at the generic user-message block (`:1423-1428`, `background: var(--v2-background-bg-layer-01)`). That is the fallback rule. The rule that actually produces the reported pairing is `:1472-1477`:

```
:root body [data-workspace-session] [data-component="user-message"] [data-slot="user-message-text"] {
  --user-message-mention-prefix-color: var(--v2-blue-300);

  background: var(--v2-background-bg-accent);
  color: var(--v2-text-text-contrast);
}
```

The fix shape is already in this file, twenty lines below. The local-session halves (`:1479-1487` light, `:1489-1497` dark) each pair a chosen background ramp with a chosen text ramp (`blue-100` on `blue-700`, `blue-1200` on `blue-300`). That is why local sessions read fine and workspace sessions do not. The workspace block is the one place that pairs a surface token with the generic contrast token without checking that the two work together. It also hardcodes `--user-message-mention-prefix-color: var(--v2-blue-300)` inside the same block, and that sits on the derived accent surface too.

Numbers, re-verified against the current head: 1.11:1 for the workspace pair, against 14.14:1 for the local pair. Ceiling: white on that accent is 2.46:1 and the surface luminance is 0.3775, so reaching 4.5:1 requires a foreground with luminance at most 0.045. Any fix that lightens the text cannot pass; the fix must go darker or change the surface.

Two shapes, both small:

1. Give the workspace-session block its own explicit pair, mirroring the local-session halves right below it. Local to one file, and it follows the pattern already established in this file.
2. Keep `text-text-contrast` for the generic case and derive an accent-surface foreground with the contrast-aware helper the icon tokens already use (`theme/v2/foreground.ts:57`). More correct, but it changes the public token surface, so per AGENTS.md it also requires re-verifying the light and dark defaults and the custom-theme fallback.

I can open the PR against either shape, whichever you prefer. The regression anchor for both is the pairing pinned by `packages/app/e2e/regression/workspace-accent.spec.ts` (assertions at `:71-79`).
